1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,300
Nine tonight? Just the event logs? Not the charts?

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:11,300
Charts stay. Those logs get overwritten unless we put a hold on them.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,200
My access ends at five. They overwrite the logs at nine. What do you need?

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,530
I can't promise which files those logs will explain.

5
00:00:30,830 --> 00:00:36,320
I need to know what might disappear. We can ask for the contents later.

6
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,970
All right. I'll send the policy.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,200
Send the log category and the policy. Only what you're allowed to see. I'll handle the rest.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,800
Am I back in the case?

9
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:07,800
No. Three other patients are filing. You're just authorizing us to use the receipt.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,300
No pictures of Ellie.

11
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:16,400
No photos. Just the receipt. You keep the original.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,350
Is this going in another story?

13
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:28,180
I'm asking about the records, not for an interview.

14
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:32,800
This goes with the formal request. Just the receipt you've authorized.

15
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:35,840
Then use that. Nothing from her folder.

16
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,300
Did they have it when they reviewed her case?

17
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:56,300
I sent it. They sent this receipt back. That's all I can sign off on.

18
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,300
Did we get them?

19
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:04,900
No. That's the filing receipt.

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,700
You've been served. The logs we need preserved are listed here.

21
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,300
Pause the job. Let me check what it covers.

22
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,800
Only these logs.

23
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:28,900
The index too. Right there.

24
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,500
That too.

25
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,750
Can the rest of the job run?

26
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:41,400
Yes. Once these exclusions are saved.

27
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:44,050
Put both categories on the confirmation.

28
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,700
The hold's in. The nine o'clock job will skip them. I'll print your confirmation.

29
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,800
Who handles the records?

30
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:12,400
Our lawyers. This just confirms the hold.

31
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,300
They saved the logs?

32
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:23,400
They're on hold. Take a look at this.

33
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:33,200
He wanted examples for appeals. That's all I knew.

34
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:38,200
They'll want every message. Let your lawyer handle it.

35
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,920
I need my pay records. The portal uses this phone.

36
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:48,360
Payroll can send them to your personal address.

37
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:53,760
Put that in the email too. And send the questions to my lawyer.

38
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:55,160
I will.

39
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:15,200
I've got the list. I'll send it. Please call before I talk to them.
